[; reference/shop/detect.cx — the DECLARED DERIVER (#865, R8.1/§4.2).

   `delayed-shipment.feature.cxd` declares

     [from 'orders/order' 'shipments/shipment']

   which since #840 IS checked (W5), and which since #865 is also the READ
   ENVELOPE of this file: shop.xap.cxd binds `detect` as the derived noun's
   one producer, and run assembly refuses a deriver whose declared reads
   escape that [from …] set. The join itself stays ordinary CX — no join
   algebra is committed by the spec:

     ON    orders/order.id = shipments/shipment.for-order
     WHERE shipments/shipment.delivered-at IS ABSENT
       AND orders/order.promised-at BEFORE now

   `delays-in` below computes it over the folded state of the two bases —
   what a real deployment runs on a timer or from a change feed — and the
   host records each result through

     [$xap:derive $rt {deriver: "detect",
                       noun: "delayed-shipment/delay-alert",
                       record: [delay-alert for-order=… customer=… promised-at=…]}]

   committing as `actor: deriver:detect` on the journal. This file was
   born as the #840 workaround feeding a hand-rolled `raise-alert` verb;
   #865 promoted it to the declared role and W7 retired the verb — the
   derivation is now the noun's ONLY producer, and it is attributable. ]

[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time' :as time]

[?def delays-in scope=public pure [returns [sequence element]] ($orders $shipments $now)
  [?for [in $o $orders]
    [; past its promise — `[$time:is-before]`, not `[<]`: ordered comparison
       is strict-numeric and refuses a date string outright, which is the
       right refusal and the wrong operator here. ]
    [where [$time:is-before [$concat '' $o/promised-at] $now]]
    [; … and no shipment for it has been delivered. `[$count]` over the
       matching-and-delivered set is the join: zero means still outstanding. ]
    [where [= [$count [?for [in $s $shipments]
                        [where [= [$concat '' $s/for-order] [$concat '' $o/id]]]
                        [where [not [= [$concat '' $s/delivered-at] '']]]
                        [yield $s]]] 0]]
    [yield [alert [for-order [$concat '' $o/id]]
                  [customer [$concat '' $o/customer]]
                  [promised-at [$concat '' $o/promised-at]]]]]]
